    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Use this tool to explore and analyse bus service distances based on scheduled data. Follow these steps to get started:</p><ol><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Select a Date Range</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Choose the period you want to analyse.</p></li><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Choose Organisations</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Filter by the relevant organisation to focus your analysis (only one organisation can be selected).</p><ol type=\"a\" style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px;\"><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Choose Operators</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Filter by relevant bus operators to focus your analysis. You can choose one or multiple operators.</p></li><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Pick Specific Services</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Select the bus services you want to examine. You can choose one or multiple services.</p></li></ol></li><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Click \"Generate\"</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Once your filters are set, click the green <strong>Generate</strong> button to view the results.</p></li><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Review the Table</p></strong><p dir=\"ltr\">The results table shows:</p><ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;\"><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Operator and Service Info</p></strong></li><li><strong><p dir=\"ltr\">Distance excluding dead runs (km)</strong> - This is the total scheduled distance for a service, based on BODS timetable data. If tracks data is available in the TransXChange files uploaded to BODS, it will be used. Otherwise, the shortest road route between stops is calculated.<br/>&#128073; We recommend uploading track data to BODS to ensure route accuracy.<br>You can view the route used for each journey on its corresponding vehicle journey page.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;\"><li><strong>Distance of journeys with AVL (km)</strong> - This is the scheduled distance for journeys where at least one GPS point was received (i.e., AVL data was available).</li><br/><li><strong>AVL Coverage (%)</strong> - This represents the percentage of the scheduled distance that had AVL data:<br><em><strong>(Distance of journeys with AVL ÷ Distance excluding dead runs) x 100</  strong></em></li></ul></li></ol>",
    "description_text": "Use this tool to explore and analyse bus service distances based on scheduled data. Follow these steps to get started:1. Select a Date Range Choose the period you want to analyse. 2. Choose Organisations: Filter by the relevant organisation to focus your analysis (only one organisation can be selected). a. Choose Operators Filter by relevant bus operators to focus your analysis. You can choose one or multiple operators. b. Pick Specific Services Select the bus services you want to examine. You can choose one or multiple services. 3. Click \"Generate\" Once your filters are set, click the green Generate button to view the results. 4. Review the Table The results table shows: 1. Operator and Service Info. 2.Distance excluding dead runs (km) – This is the total scheduled distance for a service, based on BODS timetable data. If tracks data is available in the TransXChange files uploaded to BODS, it will be used. Otherwise, the shortest road route between stops is calculated. We recommend uploading track data to BODS to ensure route accuracy. You can view the route used for each journey on its corresponding vehicle journey page. 3. Distance of journeys with AVL (km) – This is the scheduled distance for journeys where at least one GPS point was received (i.e., AVL data was available). 4. AVL Coverage (%) – This represents the percentage of the scheduled distance that had AVL data:(Distance of journeys with AVL ÷ Distance excluding dead runs) × 100",
